<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.13.1: Different Features of a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01092</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.13.1: Different Features of a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>c7ba8b44-2cf4-4c7e-8685-06fb72b2e6de</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Examine the following 4 graphs and think about why 1 of the graphs does not belong in the same group as the other 3.</para>
    <para> <figure><media alt="A graph with origin O. The graph is a line crossing the vertical axis and slants downward to cross the horizontal axis."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/16d8c744a8fb7cf5ddd315290ee08f7b4518f7d1"/></media></figure></para>
    <para><figure><media alt="A graph. "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/73a3ecbbb4cee4f09acd7c21d287c0a49ac36579"/></media></figure></para>
    <para><figure><media alt="A graph with origin O. The graph is a horizontal line passing through the middle of the vertical axis."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/d8bc94e59e979f60ffd869f1ac292c2fb21c349d"/></media></figure></para>
    <para> <figure><media alt="A graph."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eb795e5d654bbc8f6fea18c6cd13a7b8b80f997d"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Which graph does not belong? Be prepared to show your reasoning. </para>
  <para>Compare your answers:
      </para>
    Graph A doesn't belong because:
    <list>
      <item> It is the only graph that has a positive vertical intercept and a positive horizontal intercept. </item>
      <item>It is the only one that has a constant, negative rate of change.
      </item>
    </list>
    Graph B doesn't belong because:
    <list>
      <item> It is the only graph that is not a continuous curve and has multiple pieces.
      </item>
      <item>It is the only one that shows both points and lines.
      </item>
    </list>
    Graph C doesn't belong because:
    <list>
      <item> It is the only graph that has a constant y-value.
      </item>
    </list>
    Graph D doesn't belong because:
    <list>
      <item>It is the only graph whose y-value increases and decreases multiple times.
      </item>
      <item>It is the only graph that is not a simple line or curve and that has wave-like features.
      </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
